-- title:
--   Idelic reciprocity map for abelian extensions of exponent dividing 24
-- statement:
--   Let $F/E$ be a Galois extension of number fields with abelian Galois group $G=\operatorname{Gal}(F/E)$, let $\ell$ be a prime and $k$ a natural number such that $x^{\ell^k}=1$ for every $x\in G$, with $\ell^k\mid 24$ and $[F:E]\mid 24$, and let $\mathfrak f$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_E$ which is an admissible modulus for $F/E$: $\mathfrak f\neq 0$, and for every finite place $v$ of $E$ for which the inertia subgroup of $G$ at the chosen prime `primeAbove` $E$ $F$ $v$ above $v$ is nontrivial, $v^{\,4e(v\mid 2)+2e(v\mid 3)+1}$ divides $\mathfrak f$, where $e(v\mid 2)$ and $e(v\mid 3)$ denote the ramification indices of $v$ over the ideals generated by $2$ and by $3$. Then there exists a group homomorphism $r$ from the idèle group $(\mathbb A_E)^\times$ to $G$ such that: the subgroup of principal idèles, i.e. the image of $E^\times$ under the map induced by $E\to\mathbb A_E$, lies in $\ker r$; $\ker r$ equals the join of the principal idèles with the image of the idelic norm $(\mathbb A_F)^\times\to(\mathbb A_E)^\times$ obtained by applying `Algebra.norm` for the base-change `genuineBaseChange` $E$ $F$ of adèle rings; $r$ is surjective; and for every idèle $u$ which is a $1$-adjuster at $\mathfrak f$, meaning that at each $v\mid\mathfrak f$ the finite component $u_v$ has valuation $1$ and $u_v-1$ has valuation at most $\exp(-n_v)$ with $n_v$ the multiplicity of $v$ in $\mathfrak f$, and that the real projection of $u$ at each real embedding of $E$ is positive, one has $r(u)=\prod^{\mathrm f}_{v}\,\mathrm{Frob}_v^{\;\mathrm{ord}_v(u_v)}$, the finitely supported product over all finite places $v$ of $E$ of the arithmetic Frobenius at `primeAbove` $E$ $F$ $v$ raised to $-\log$ of the valuation of the $v$-component of the finite part of $u$.
--
--   This is the global reciprocity law for abelian extensions, in the restricted range where both the exponent of the Galois group and the degree divide $24$, packaged as an idelic Artin map: trivial on principal idèles, with kernel the product of the principal idèles and the idelic norms, surjective, and computed as a product of Frobenius elements on idèles adjusted to be trivial at the modulus. It feeds the construction of resolvent characters in the cubic-resolvent step of the Langlands–Tunnell input.
